From f666739131aebdba96c95bba68be7f4c43b21157 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:51:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Aurora: Wind Waker HD's bloom, SSAO, rim light, cloud shadows
 and shadow pass

Each behind its own switch, off by default, from HD's own shaders and RenderDoc captures of Cemu:

- DOL_AURORA_BLOOM_HD: HD's bloom chain (detect at a quarter size x 0.65, three levels at 1/8, 1/16 and 1/32
  blurred by HD's 13-tap Gaussian, tinted, gathered and screened); _MASK adds HD's mask from the sea mask's
  pass (only what writes no depth glows: the sky).
- DOL_AURORA_AO_HD: HD's SSAO in the terrain mix's pass, on the scenery's shade alone.
- DOL_AURORA_RIM_HD: HD's rim light on toon-shaded characters, from the mask's green and the characters' own
  normals (green 1 for toon-shaded characters, 0.6 for skinned-only draws).
- DOL_AURORA_CLOUD_SHADOWS_HD: cloud shadows on HD's rule (they take away the sun's light, floor
  1 - 0.9 x the sun's height), with HD's own ww_shadow_clouds (a BC4 DDS, repeat every 15,000 units, drifting
  0.01116 a second): from DOL_AURORA_CLOUD_SHADOWS_HD_TEXTURE or the host (aurora_set_hd_cloud_texture, the
  HD pack's optional/hd-cloud-shadow/ww_shadow_clouds.dds).
- The "hd" shadow quality (DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_QUALITY=hd, set_sun_shadow_quality(3)): HD's shadow pass,
  three 1024 cascades, a half-size pre-pass with one filtered lookup per pixel in the cascade its distance
  picks, blurred with HD's 3-tap Gaussian, every pixel's shadow from it; the sea's shadow at HD's half
  strength.
- Characters keep BlueWake's caster bias (with HD's, Link's shadow came off his feet;
  _CASTER_BIAS_CHARACTERS=1 gives them HD's) and slope term; the HD mix's near power is
  DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_HD_MIX_NEAR_POWER.
- DOL_AURORA_WINDOW_NO_ACTIVATE=1, for scripted runs while someone uses the machine: the window opens behind
  what has the focus.
